    "title": "fix: preserve percent-encoded path in DisplayURL",
    "url": "https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/13788",
    "state": "OPEN",
    "isDraft": false,
    "author": {
     "login": "user-2",
     "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1?v=4"
    },
    "bodyHTML": "<h2 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #13546.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4549277326\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/cli/cli/issues/13546\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/cli/cli/issues/13546/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/cli/cli/issues/13546\">#13546</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">DisplayURL</code> was using <code class=\"notranslate\">u.Path</code> which is the unescaped version of the URL path. This caused branch names with special characters (like quotes) to be displayed incorrectly in the terminal when using <code class=\"notranslate\">gh pr create --web</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">For example, a branch named <code class=\"notranslate\">test-\"quoted\"-branch-pr</code> would display as:</p>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"https://github.com/OWNER/REPO/compare/...test-&quot;quoted&quot;-branch-pr\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">https://github.com/OWNER/REPO/compare/...test-\"quoted\"-branch-pr\n</code></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Instead of the correct:</p>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"https://github.com/OWNER/REPO/compare/...test-%22quoted%22-branch-pr\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">https://github.com/OWNER/REPO/compare/...test-%22quoted%22-branch-pr\n</code></pre></div>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Changes</h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Uses <code class=\"notranslate\">u.RawPath</code> (when available) instead of <code class=\"notranslate\">u.Path</code> to preserve the original percent-encoding from the URL.</p>",
