          "author": {
           "login": "user-3",
           "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2?v=4"
          },
          "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">u.RawPath is only populated when the raw path differs from the default escaping of u.Path, so this misses the common case. e.g. <a href=\"https://x/a%20b\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://x/a%20b</a> decodes Path to \"a b\" whose canonical escape is \"a%20b\", which matches raw, so RawPath stays \"\" and you fall back to the decoded Path. u.EscapedPath() handles both and is what you want here.</p>",
          "createdAt": "2026-07-21T04:26:13Z",
          "url": "https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/13788#discussion_r3619422472",
          "state": "SUBMITTED",
          "diffHunk": "@@ -77,7 +77,12 @@ func DisplayURL(urlStr string) string {\n \tif scheme == \"\" {\n \t\tscheme = \"https\"\n \t}\n-\treturn scheme + \"://\" + u.Hostname() + u.Path\n+\tpath := u.Path\n+\t// Preserve percent-encoding from the original URL path\n+\tif u.RawPath != \"\" {\n+\t\tpath = u.RawPath\n+\t}",
          "originalCommit": {
           "oid": "2537a3b6931a787d6b4b0ab686cd4cf7eda0dfda"
          },
          "pullRequestReview": {
           "id": "PRR_kwDODKw3uc8AAAABGplw5Q"
          }
         }
        ]
       }
      }
     ]
